Near-misses for diag.hungarian_type_mismatch: matching builtin return
types, NIL, unknown right-hand sides (user procedure, array element,
v-prefixed name), unprefixed targets, compound assignment, a member
target, and an operand pair with no documented result (aList + sText).
That last line is still diag.mixed_type_operator's finding (array + string)
under every profile, which is correct for that rule.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Refresh;
	:PARAMETERS sText, aList, vAny;
	:DECLARE nCode, dStart, aNames, oRec, Total, i;
	nCode := Len(sText);
	sText := AllTrim(sText);
	dStart := Today();
	aNames := {"Ann", "Bob"};
	oRec := CreateUdObject();
	sText := NIL;
	nCode := DoProc("LookupCode", {sText});
	nCode := aList[1];
	nCode := vAny;
	Total := "anything";
	i := "counter";
	nCode += 1;
	oRec:sLabel := 5;
	nCode := aList + sText;
	:RETURN {nCode, dStart, aNames, oRec, Total, i};
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics [--hungarian-types] --
17:17-17:18 warning mixed_type_operator: Mixed types in '+' operation: array + string. The '+' operator requires both operands to be the same type (both strings or both numeric)
